      "problem": "Given the ellipsoid $\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{4}=1$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(0-1)^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{4} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ (x-2)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x-2 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ x & =2\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $x=0$ and $x=4.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(4,0,0).$",
